  "readmeSummary": "## Instagram Scraper\n\nInstagram Scraper extracts public Instagram content and metadata across posts, carousels, reels, comments, mentions, profiles, hashtags, and places. It scrapes media and contextual data including captions, hashtags, @-mentions, image and video URLs, thumbnails and profile pictures, carousel children, audio/music metadata, media dimensions and durations, timestamps, and owner/profile metadata (bio, full name, follower/following counts, verified/business flags). Engagement and performance metrics returned include likes, comment counts, views/plays, comment text with author identity and reply threads, and hashtag analytics such as post counts, posts-per-day, related-tag clusters and reach tiers. Place/location outputs include coordinates, address, category, post counts and top/latest posts. The Actor supports discovery by keyword search (profiles, hashtags, places) or scraping from lists of URLs, and offers features like date filtering, content-type selection (posts vs reels vs comments vs mentions vs details), pinned-post handling, and nested comment retrieval. Outputs are structured, record-oriented datasets of media, engagement, profile, hashtag, mention, comment and place metadata suitable for trend analysis, influencer evaluation, brand monitoring, and other downstream analytics.\n\n## Use cases\n\n- Influencer vetting and partnership research (creator discovery, engagement scoring, audience audit)\n- Trend tracking and UGC intelligence (hashtag trend monitoring, adjacent tag discovery)\n- Competition and campaign monitoring (content performance comparison, posting cadence analysis)\n- Brand monitoring and mentions (caption mentions, branded hashtag UGC, @-tag collection)\n- Local business discovery and lead generation (place discovery by category + city, business profile enrichment)\n- Content and image analysis (media URLs, captions, alt text, audio/music metadata)\n- UGC discovery and sentiment analysis (comments, replies, author identities, timestamps)\n- Campaign performance tracking (likes, comments, views, plays, timestamps)",
